# Candidate only. Every non-baseline line must be tested as a one-variable ablation.
# Its one change, max-num-seqs 256 -> 96, cannot change scheduling: each
# conversation has at most one request in flight, so any value >= 70 never
# makes a request wait. It only shrinks the CUDA Graph capture range
# (2 x max-num-seqs in vLLM 0.25.1) and memory reservation.
LiquidAI/LFM2.5-1.2B-Instruct
--max-model-len=8192
--gpu-memory-utilization=0.95
--tensor-parallel-size=1
--enable-prefix-caching
--quantization=fp8
--kv-cache-dtype=fp8
--optimization-level=3
--max-num-seqs=96
--max-num-batched-tokens=8192
